{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793696545,"nonce":"8Ju81c4F21KEEDMuLURuoVV2XFg=","title":"Converge blinc_css and blinc_abi::css: where they diverge, and the order to close it","message":"Context (owner, 2026-11-03): blinc_abi::css exists because the agents on blinc_abi did not want to change Blinc's CSS and layout architecture. The divergence is accidental, so this is a convergence plan, not a choice between two designs. Related: 5e711e5 (DSL on blinc_abi), 6f7b001 (engine model). Facts are measured with a probe that asks both engines about the same properties and declarations; the 8-bit colour quantisation and host-routed text properties are noted where they limit a comparison.\n\nShape of each engine\n\n- blinc_css (Blinc, 22.0k lines): nom parsers into a typed ElementStyle; depends on blinc_animation and blinc_theme; value parsing needs ThemeState initialised (it panics without). Selector matching and the cascade live elsewhere, in blinc_layout's renderer/stylesheet (5.1k lines). Own subsystems: @flow shader DAGs (1.4k), keyframes and animation parsing (1.0k), materials and glass (0.6k), 3D (shape-3d, perspective, rotate-x/y, translate-z, lights, surfaces), calc (1.2k), pointer spaces, image placeholders, the ElementStyle builders and css!/style! macros (5.4k), theme() references.\n- blinc_abi::css (16.4k lines, 8.5k of it non-test grammar): hand-written parser, arena stylesheet with interned atoms, a compiled byte form, a cascade over a host-agnostic Tree trait (specificity, !important, @layer, media, containers, :has), typed paint and layout writes. Serves ashui and blinc_ts, so it carries the full web grammar. Own subsystems: @font-face, @media, @supports, @container, @import with a loader, @mixin/@include, nesting with \u0026, generated content (::before/::after), :nth-*/:not/:is/:where/:has, compiled sheets, JSON dump.\n\nProperties\n- 99 known to both, 60 only to blinc_css, 24 only to blinc_abi (host-read text properties are not counted for the ABI, so its side is a lower bound).\n- Only blinc_css: animation and transition (parsed; the ABI leaves motion to each SDK), SVG fill and stroke*, 3D and materials (perspective, rotate-x/y, translate-z, shape-*, depth, light-*, surface-*, specular, ambient, render-layer), pointer-*, image-placeholder-*, accent-color, caret-color, mix-blend-mode, object-fit, mask-mode, scrollbar-width, skew-x/y.\n- Only blinc_abi: flex (shorthand), order, aspect-ratio, align-content, justify-items, justify-self, background-image, background-size, background-position, background-repeat, line-clamp, text-decoration-style, text-underline-offset, glass-*.\n\nAt-rules and selectors\n- blinc_css reads @keyframes, @flow, :root variables and one @layer block; it has none of @media, @supports, @container, @import, @font-face, @mixin, nesting.\n- Selectors are close: types, ids, classes, attributes with every operator, the four combinators, :nth-*, :not, :is, :where, :has, the states.\n\nValues, where both engines know the property (160 hand-built cases plus 385 real declarations)\n- Real stylesheets: 331 of 340 declarations agree. cn and the UA sheet through the ABI: 314 of 380 accepted, 57 not routed by the ABI (text properties, animation, transition), 9 rejected (translate(100%) and its three siblings, once each in two forms, and one theme()). ashui's through blinc_css: 1,516 of 1,525 accepted.\n- blinc_css is narrower on standard CSS: no em, rem, vw, vh, vmin or vmax; no min(), max() or clamp(); no percentage padding or inset; no auto insets; no two-value gap; no z-index auto; no multi-value border-color; no matrix(); no grad angles; no url/position/size in the background shorthand.\n- blinc_abi is narrower on Blinc's extras: no theme(token) (themes arrive as var(--token) through set_theme), no fit-content or max-content, no translate(%) (resolved when an animation starts in Blinc), no 3D transforms (rotateX/Y, perspective()), no percentage border-radius, no calc() in opacity, no url() in mask-image.\n- blinc_css is also more lenient where CSS is not: min-width: none is accepted.\n\nConverged today\n- blinc_css colours follow CSS and agree with the ABI on every syntax probed: 4-digit hex, rgb() and hsl() in comma and space forms with / alpha, percentages, hue units, all 148 named colours. This fixes a bug: rgb(1, 1, 1) came out white because components at or under 1 were read as fractions; named colours now take their CSS values (orange is #ffa500, not Color::ORANGE). No CSS in the repository relied on it; the 8-bit tests are in blinc_css.\n- blinc_abi accepts max-width and max-height: none.\n- cn's one theme(shadow-sm) is var(--shadow-sm); the tabs golden is unchanged.\n- A conformance ledger (crates/blinc_css/tests/conformance/values.tsv) records each case's verdict from each engine and is checked by a test in both repos, so a gap cannot close or open unnoticed.\n\nOrder to close the rest\n1. A shared value grammar. The ABI's value modules (color, calc, gradient, transform, filter, shadow, clip_path, border, text_decoration, quantity, value, svg_path) are pure functions over blinc_core types. Move them into one Blinc crate that both blinc_css and blinc_abi depend on: blinc_abi already depends on Blinc by git URL, so this adds no cycle. blinc_abi re-exports them at their old paths so ashui and blinc_ts are unaffected. Blinc's extras (theme(), 3D, materials, flow) stay in blinc_css as extensions over the shared grammar. Each module moves with its tests and its ledger rows turning to agree.\n2. The units and math Blinc lacks (em, rem, vw, vh, min/max/clamp, percentage lengths) arrive with step 1 for calc and quantity, then fill the ElementStyle and layout gaps (flex shorthand, order, aspect-ratio, align-content, justify-*, background-image/size/position/repeat, line-clamp, text-decoration-style and offset).\n3. The ABI gains what Blinc has: translate(%), percentage radii, intrinsic sizing keywords, theme() as an alias of var(), and the 3D and material extensions (a record version bump, see 5e711e5).\n4. At-rules and the cascade: blinc_layout's matcher (5.1k lines) and the ABI cascade are the same job done twice; converge on one, and bring @media, @supports, @container, @import, @font-face, nesting to the Blinc side with it. This is the 6f7b001 step and the largest.\n5. Motion: the ABI has none (36603e0).\n\nOwner decisions\n- Endpoint: one grammar crate under both engines (above), then one cascade; or blinc_layout adopts blinc_abi::css wholesale. I recommend the grammar crate first either way, because each step is reversible and gated by the ledger.\n- Whether the legacy rgb() fractions dialect (rgb(0.2, 0.4, 0.9)) needs a compatibility path; none in this repository uses it.\n\nNot established: var() with fallback chains across the two engines (the corpora excluded var()); selector matching differences (only grammar was compared); performance.","files":null}]}